{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512221-werewols-countering-obfuscate-and-presence","id":1512221,"title":"Werewols countering Obfuscate and Presence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-20T09:45:41-07:00","id":1512221,"title":"Werewols countering Obfuscate and Presence","content":"Are there any any Gifts, Fetishes ect. that allow Werewolfs to counter or be more resistant against Obfuscate and Presence or other powers based on illusion or emotional manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T11:22:57-07:00","id":1512226,"title":"","content":"NB: All of this pertains to pre-W5 (rather obviously, but still).<br /> <br /> A Rank 3 Crinos-born Gift, Shell, can shut out Presence at the cost of cutting off Rage while in use. The Nagah have a bunch of Gifts and even a Fetish for emotional and illusion defense.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate can be defeated by simultaneous observation of the Middle Umbra and physical realm, as it doesn't extend into the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, having a high Rage can make Presence a tricky thing to use on you, as it can frequently trigger frenzies and any kind of fear effect, per Werewolf the Dark Ages (the softcover), anything that requires Courage to resist in Vampire defaults to going against Rage instead (Willpower can also be used, if higher). Shadow Lords and Ananasi can also pay the vampires back the favor with their own Presence-like Gift effects; Icy Chill of Despair isn't always on, but its mechanics are very similar to Presence 5 (Level 3 for Shadow Lords, or a starting Gift for Ananasi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T11:52:14-07:00","id":1512231,"title":"","content":"I feel like I read somewhere that werewolves just contest with perception + primal urge but I may be mistaken. There are powers like Ears of the Bat that directly deal with obfuscate. You could also enlist a spirit, immune to the mind altering powers of Garou (not Presence, but Obfuscate and Dominate certainly) to help locate things. <br /> <br /> It should also be noted that obfuscate has a range and wolves have an incredible sense of hearing and smell. If they discover the vampire before entering the range then the only method to become hidden is to use obfuscate 4 when the wolves have re-entered range. I suppose Obfuscate 3 could be attempted if the werewolves didn't see the target but could smell/hear it, if appearing to be some-other vampire could do you any favours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T12:42:28-07:00","id":1512235,"title":"","content":"Heightened Senses, I can't believe that I forgot it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T10:18:33-07:00","id":1512291,"title":"","content":"Noticing an invisible supernatural threat is classic Primal-Urge stuff, though noticing isn't the same as overcoming of course! Typically a Garou who gets a hint of an invisible danger will simply be aware that something is wrong. They may then attempt to use a Gift like Sense Wyrm, which could help them find the Vampire if the Vampire's Humanity is 6 or lower. There are also other Gifts like Heightened Senses, Scent of Sight etc. which could help overcome Obfuscate. As always compare power levels and consider having a resisted roll etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T10:23:06-07:00","id":1512365,"title":"","content":"Do you thing the Nagah Gift Pierce Illusion (Changing Breeds page 161) would also work against Obfuscate or only against Chimerstry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T17:44:10-07:00","id":1512509,"title":"","content":"The 1999 sourcebook Werewolf: the Dark Ages gives some guidance on this. Here are some of its suggestions:<br /> <br /> Obfuscate does not affect Garou in the Penumbra who peek into the Realm.<br /> <br /> Sensory Gifts like Sense Wyrm, Heightened Senses, etc. can detect something is amiss, but not what exactly is wrong. I interpret that to mean it cannot &quot;pierce&quot; Obfuscate, but it detects - in some vague fashion - that something unnatural is affecting the Garou. But it cannot pinpoint the source of the user or that this is a vampire doing it.<br /> <br /> Presence works as normal, but a vampire attempting to use it on a frenzying werewolf had additional difficulty. To resist, Werewolves can roll Willpower rather then their Courage.<br /> <br /> The Silver Fang Gift: Mindblock raises difficulty to 10 for mind affecting powers like Obfuscate, Presence, and Dominate.<br /> <br /> If you want to use this as a guide, you can probably figure out anything else that is applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T22:21:13-07:00","id":1512544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512221-werewols-countering-obfuscate-and-presence?p=1512509#post1512509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Fang Gift: Mindblock raises difficulty to 10 for mind affecting powers like Obfuscate, Presence, and Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the current version of Mindblock does rule out Presence, that was why I was wondering if there was some equivalent for it that works against Presence but not Dominate (in Vampire you often see a split like that).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T07:31:35-07:00","id":1512955,"title":"","content":"In the w20 p.273 there's a table for the use of werewolve's sense that tell they can detect object/people hidden by a power (Perception + alertness/primal urge difficulty 8) so i think they can detect a vampire hidden by obfuscate. In addition that difficulty drop by 2 while in lupus form, wich seems to be in the line with the animal 6th sense stuff. Of course the ST could state that obfuscate affect their sense normally, but it would be hard to affect werewolf primal urge in my oppinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 05-27-2023, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T23:24:43-07:00","id":1513746,"title":"","content":"I've similarly used this as a Primal-Urge sensing roll at difficulty 8+ where success indicated a 100\u00b0 cone in which the garou could tell that there was something suspicious there, and a successful perception alertness told them that they couldn't see/smell/hear anything suspicious in the same space. <br /> <br /> The malkavian in question took it as a good opportunity to heighten the paranoia of the lupine, wait for it to start looking around for an ambush and make his escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}